r side wants to pass  legislation to ensure  everyone who's entitled to vote can vote  they're both  simply partisan voting rights  pieces of legislation this is it's hard  to imagine  a more depraved sort of both sides  type argument and this is exactly  what i feared would happen with joe  manchin  and it is indeed happening huffington  post is also  reporting about this saying that senator  joe manchin said he won't vote  for his parties for the people act a  bill focused on expanding voting rights  again the idea that  limiting voting rights which is against  the constitution against the law against  what this country is built on  and expanding voting rights for people  who can legally vote  are just two sides of the same political  coin  that is the full end position  toxicity level of the idea of the  enlightened centrist and i'm not going  to be super partisan on either side  when one side is trying to take rights  away you can't say well  i don't want to get involved on this  side either because we're just as  partisan in trying to make sure people  have their rights that's not the way it  works  and this is the sort of you know i i use  the term enlightened centrism  sometimes to refer to online  commentators or whatever who  want to pretend to kind of be above the  partisan fray and see both sides  but this is one of 100 members of the  u.s  senate who is equating taking voting  rights away  as a partisan act by republicans to  giving voting rights as a partisan act  by democrats when the reality is  what the constitution says and what the  law says should be the guiding principle  here so it's  truly unbelievable and disgusting uh  kirsten cinema  on the democratic side also arguably a  problem uh in  in some areas and we'll ultimately see  what happens with this  uh for for the people act but this does  not look  good now i i know that many people will  say well david then  let's primary joe manchin i'm not  against primary anybody as i've said  before  